@bank all
// SW2, 0.92.6 item 4 (FX17's word list): Reading corner, Sundays 16:00-17:00 in the bow lounge armchairs; host Esme
// Walsh (galley, late team; off at weekends: quiet, exact, minutes and grams, never "a bit"). Goers sit close on the
// couches and seats and talk about the book they're reading. Keys, as FX17 named them:
//   reading.welcome  Esme opens (90 or fewer).       reading.wrap   Esme closes.
//   reading.titles   12 invented books, one title per line. Data: FX17 hands one to each reader as {title}.
//   reading.book     any reader, Esme too, on their book (bubbles, 60 or fewer with the longest title in).
//   reading.reply    someone answering a reader (bubbles, 60 or fewer).
// Titles name only canon places (Coriel); nothing real.

== reading.welcome
- Hello. Armchairs are free, books are on the shelf. Sit close. Talk quietly.
- Reading corner. Sixty minutes. Pull your chair in, and tell us what you're reading.
- Come in. Tea's poured, two hundred millilitres each. Pick a chair. Pick a book.   #funny
== reading.wrap
- That's sixty minutes. Shelf books back where they live, please. Thank you.
- Time. Spines out on the shelf. Same chairs next Sunday, if you like.   #warm

== reading.titles
- The Lighthouse at Coriel
- Tea for the Night Watch
- A Hundred Small Repairs
- Bread on Sundays
- Rain on the Harbour Wall
- The Long Way Round
- Small Hours
- The Quiet Star
- Soup for the Way Home
- What the Coil Said
- The Last Ferry Home
- A Map of Grey Skies

== reading.book
- I'm on {title}. Can't put it down.
- {title}. Third time. Still gets me.   #warm
- Reading {title}. The ending's coming.
- {title}. Slow start. Worth it.
- I'm halfway through {title}.
- {title}. Off the lounge shelf.
- Has anyone read {title}? No spoilers.
- {title}. Reading it slowly, on purpose.
- {title} has the best first page.
- Reading {title} aloud. In my head.   #funny
- Started {title} last night. Up too late.   #funny
- {title}. Short chapters. Dangerous.   #funny
- {title}. It's about a ship like ours.
- {title}. I keep reading bits to my bunkmates.   #funny
- {title}. Somebody's underlined things.
- {title}. Is it sad? Tell me it's not.
- {title}. Smells like the lounge shelf.
- Back on {title}. Lost my place twice.   #funny
- {title}. The cook in it is wonderful.
- {title}. My third Sunday on it.

== reading.reply
- Ooh, I loved that one.
- Lend it me after?
- Read that one twice. Wait for chapter nine.
- No spoilers. I'm next on the list for it.
- That one's on my shelf. Still unread.   #funny
- The ending. Oh, the ending.   #warm
- Is it good? It looks good.
- Read me the first line?
